From d6d80a4f65f5d1fc657e8a49009b788048157d17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 23:26:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: sun6i-isp: Describe what the white balance window
 actually sets

The window is not the region measured. It gives the size of one cell,
and the grid of sixteen by twelve cells is what spans the frame, so the
measured extent is four times the width by six times the height.

Measured across nine widths and nine heights with closing brackets: the
total over the 32 written records is 4 * width * height to the pixel,
until the grid runs off the frame. That happens at a quarter of the
frame width and a sixth of its height, 400 by 200 on a 1600 by 1200
sensor, and both limits land exactly where the counts stop tracking --
384 works and 416 does not, 192 works and 208 does not. The grid is 16
by 12 against a frame of 1600 by 1200, the same 4:3, so a window at the
limit tiles the frame exactly and one past it cannot.

The limit is on the extent alone: repeating the sweep with the window
origin at 800 instead of 0 breaks at the same width, so the layout
ignores where the window starts.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 .../media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
index 2c50b2b10d63..8b24457c1079 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
@@ -306,11 +306,16 @@ struct sun6i_isp_stats_afs {
  *
  * The array is sized for the region the hardware is given, but only the
  * first 32 records are populated on the A83T; the rest are zeroed, so
- * the vendor's own count test rejects them. The populated records form
- * a grid eight columns wide whose cell size follows the programmed
- * window, exactly, up to a window 384 pixels wide -- beyond that the
- * relation breaks down and is not yet understood, so treat a wide
- * window's numbers as unreliable rather than as a measurement.
+ * the vendor's own count test rejects them. Those 32 are sixteen
+ * columns by two rows.
+ *
+ * The window here is not the region measured. It gives the size of one
+ * cell, and the grid of 16 by 12 cells is what spans the frame, so the
+ * measured extent is four times the width by six times the height. A
+ * window larger than a quarter of the frame width or a sixth of its
+ * height therefore runs the grid off the frame and the counts stop
+ * meaning anything -- 400 by 200 against a 1600 by 1200 sensor. Nothing
+ * range-checks this.
  */
 struct sun6i_isp_stats_awb_window {
 	__u32	sum[3];
-- 
2.43.0

